# ===========================================================================
# Dokploy services: medusa-postgres + medusa-redis
#
# Create these as native Dokploy DATABASES (Project -> Create -> Database),
# not as compose services. You then get automated S3 backups, monitoring and
# a managed volume for free.
# ===========================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Postgres
# Dokploy -> Create -> Database -> Postgres
#   Name          : medusa-postgres
#   Docker Image  : postgres:16-alpine
POSTGRES_USER=medusa
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
POSTGRES_DB=medusa

# After creating it, open the Database -> "Internal Host" / "Internal
# Connection URL" and paste that value into DATABASE_URL on BOTH backend
# services. Leave "External Port" unset unless you need remote psql access.
#
# Expected shape:
#   postgres://medusa:CHANGE_ME@medusa-postgres:5432/medusa

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- Redis
# Dokploy -> Create -> Database -> Redis
#   Name          : medusa-redis
#   Docker Image  : redis:7-alpine
REDIS_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME

# Paste the Internal Connection URL into REDIS_URL on BOTH backend services.
#
# Expected shape:
#   redis://default:CHANGE_ME@medusa-redis:6379
#
# Redis is required in production: it backs the caching, event bus, workflow
# engine and locking modules that let backend-server and backend-worker
# coordinate. Without it each instance would run its own in-memory queue and
# jobs would double-fire.

# ---------------------------------------------------------- Meilisearch (NOT a Database)
# Meilisearch runs as an Application (NOT a native Dokploy Database — see
# deploy/meilisearch/Dockerfile + env/meilisearch.env.example). Paste the
# Application's internal App Name and master key into MEILISEARCH_HOST /
# MEILISEARCH_API_KEY on BOTH backend services.
#
# Expected shape:
#   MEILISEARCH_HOST=http://medusa-meilisearch-<suffix>:7700
#   MEILISEARCH_API_KEY=<MEILI_MASTER_KEY from env/meilisearch.env.example>
#   MEILISEARCH_PRODUCT_INDEX_NAME=products
